# Mission 1: HUD System Health Widget

## Goal
Add a real-time "System Health" indicator to the Nucleus HUD.
This satisfies Pillar 2 (Visibility) of the Strategy.

## User Review Required
None. Internal Mission.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend
#### [MODIFY] [server.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/server.py)
- Add conditional for `/api/health`.
- Return `{"status": "green", "uptime": <seconds>, "version": "1.0"}`.

### Frontend
#### [NEW] [SystemHealth.tsx](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/app/components/SystemHealth.tsx)
- React component.
- Polls `/api/health` every 5 seconds.
- Displays Green Dot / Red Dot.

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/app/page.tsx)
- Import `SystemHealth`.
- Add to the Grid layout (top right?).

## Verification Plan
### Automated Tests
- `curl http://localhost:9999/api/health` -> 200 OK.
### Manual Verification
- Open HUD.
- See Green Dot.
- Kill backend -> See Red Dot.
